    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        470,
        780
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        220
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 25,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "Why one model chain",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Shared model chain\n\nLoRA -> SigmaShift(12,3) -> Timeline Model Patch -> AttentionBackend, in that order -- feeds BOTH passes' guiders and the pass-1 scheduler. The 8-step schedule below is only correct for THIS LoRA; a different step-distilled checkpoint needs a different split boundary and refine sigmas."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1360,
        1320
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        260
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 26,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "One node, matched pair",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### The two-pass join\n\nUpscales the AV latent AND carries the keyframe conditioning to the new canvas, as one node -- the two outputs can't disagree about the canvas because they come from the same place.\n\nReplaces LTXVSeparateAVLatent -> upscaler -> LTXVConcatAVLatent AND a second Conditioning node."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        900,
        1560
      ],
      "size": [
        300,
        220
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 27,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "Don't substitute a generic scheduler",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Pass 2 sigmas\n\n`0.9035, 0.6316, 0.3158, 0.0000` is NOT a generic partial-denoise fraction -- it's a hand-tuned tail for this specific LoRA + sigma shift. A BasicScheduler(steps, denoise<1) on the plain model here produces visibly worse output; confirmed directly."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
